'' sys/win IS WINDOWS-ONLY, and says so: every sys/win module's header opens with
'' '#ifndef TIKO_OS_WINDOWS / #error', so an import for linux-x86_64 fails on that line first
'' rather than somewhere inside windows.bi.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-x86_64 -c tests/modules/src/syswinguard/main.tiko -o build/.syswinguard.o
'' ENV: TIKO_INCLUDE=toolchains/tiko-windows/inc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: win.ti(3,1): error TKO0309: #error: "sys/win is Windows-only: build for -target windows-x86_64"
